       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual 400\u2013800 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), for typical pain or fever\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided as 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want the dose as written, please confirm it. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first. Once you tell me the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
